  "slug": "energy-audit-incident-report-form",
  "title": "Energy Audit Incident Report Form",
  "subtitle": "An original energy audit workflow that captures an event from emergency routing through corrective-action closeout, with explicit qualified-review, stop-work, escalation, and accountable handoff controls.",
  "description": "A workflow-complete energy audit incident report form for the building energy-use assessment that captures exact identity, domain observations, supporting evidence, decisions, exceptions, responsible owners, and closeout without replacing professional judgment or the organization's controlling procedures.",
  "use_case": "Use after an incident or near miss to record safe initial facts, consequences, chronology, evidence custody, scene restrictions, notifications, qualified review, corrective actions, and final handoff. The energy assessment lead owns routing, and closure requires documented evidence, disposition of restrictions, and acceptance by the designated reviewer.",
  "risk_tier": "C",
  "sections": [
    {
